        "agm_place": "Gedung Bank Panin Pusat, Lantai 4, JL. Jend. Sudirman Kav.1, Gelora, Tanah Abang, Jakartapusat, 10270",
        "agm_result": "Agenda #1: The meeting approved the 2025 Annual Report and Financial Statements, granting a full discharge of responsibility to the Board of Directors and Commissioners.\nAgenda #2: Shareholders approved the allocation of Rp212,215,700,804 in net profit for general reserves, cash dividends of Rp50 per share, and retained earnings.\nAgenda #3: The meeting accepted Harjanto Tjitohardjojo's resignation and appointed Jahja Anwar as President Director, along with Lie Roelly Makalis and Willy Halim Sugiardi as Directors until 2029.\nAgenda #4: Authority was granted to the majority shareholder to determine honorariums for the Board of Commissioners and to the Board of Commissioners to set salaries for the Board of Directors for the 2026 fiscal year.\nAgenda #5: The Board of Commissioners was delegated the authority to select and appoint an independent Public Accountant or Public Accounting Firm to audit the 2026 fiscal year financial statements.\nAgenda #6: The proposal to amend the Articles of Association was not approved because the required attendance quorum was not met.\nAgenda #7: The proposal to guarantee more than 50% of the company's net assets for loan facilities was not approved due to an insufficient attendance quorum."
      },
      {
        "agm_date": "2026-07-09",
        "agm_time": "10:00:00",
        "agm_place": "Gedung Bank Panin Pusat Lantai 4 Jl. Jend. Sudirman Kav.1, Gelora, Tanah Abang",
        "agm_result": "Agenda #1: Approval of amendments to the Company's Articles of Association to align with the 2025 Indonesian Standard Industrial Classification (KBLI) code, specifically amending Article 3, Section 3.3, and approving the revised Articles in their entirety. The decision was approved by shareholders.\nAgenda #2: Granting authority to the Board of Directors or Mr. Lie Roelly Makalis to restate the Company's Articles of Association in a notarial deed, submit applications for approval of amendments, and take necessary actions, with conditions including the right to transfer the power and effectiveness from the adjournment of the GMS.\nAgenda #3: Approval of the Company providing guarantees of more than 50% or all of its net worth to obtain loans from government agencies, banks, non-bank financial institutions, or through public offerings of non-equity securities, for fiscal years 2027 through 2029. The decision was approved by shareholders."
      }
